WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:16.000
For this project you will need the printed copy of the template, scissors and tape.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.540
Cut out the five strips on the dotted line.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.820
Make sure to separate the co-joined strips.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.100
The green, orange and yellow tabs have to remain attached to their respective strips.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.040
Proteins are polymer chains of amino acid residues.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.420
Each number on the model represents one amino acid residue.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.240
Insulin has two chains. Chain A, is green Chain B is blue.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:50.989
Tape together the two pieces of the A chain (green) so that residue 11 is back-to-back in the two pieces.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:58.309
Tape together the three pieces of the B chain (blue) by overlapping the gray tabs at the ends, so that

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:00.799
all the numbers are visible on one side and all the numbers are in order.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.940
Some sections of amino acid chains 
curl and form alpha helices due 
to hydrogen bonds between N-H and C-O groups.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:20.920
The helix regions on the model are marked on the chains with darker shades of green and blue.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:28.240
Starting with residues 1 and 5 form a hydrogen bond between C-O and N-H, and tape together.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:36.120
Keep creating the hydrogen bonds until you reach the end of the darker colored area.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.460
When you reach residue 6, make sure the green tab is on the outside of the helix.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:47.880
Create another alpha helix starting with residues 17 and 21.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.249
Keep creating hydrogen bonds until you reach the end of the darker colored area.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:13.779
Starting with residues 7 and 11, form a hydrogen bond.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.199
Keep creating the alpha helix until you reach the end of the darker colored area.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:37.870
Some amino acids give a TURN to the chain. 
The turns are marked on chain B of the 
paper model with the white dashed lines.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:43.630
Fold outwards on the white dashed lines to create the turns. You can secure the folds with tape.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:50.350
Also note that chain B also includes a beta strand marked with a blue arrow.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.570
The structure of Insulin is stabilized by 3 disulfide bridges.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.690
A disulfide bridge is formed when a sulfur atom from the residue cysteine

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:09.520
forms a single covalent bond with a sulfur atom from a second cysteine.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:17.529
The first disulfide bridge connects 2 
cysteines in chain A. To form the bridge, connect the green tabs

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:26.889
Connect the yellow tabs, matching their shape while making sure the colored sides are facing the same way.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:38.609
Connect the orange tabs matching their shape while making sure the colored sides are facing the same way.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:55.320
Congratulations! If you have completed all the steps and your project looks like the one shown here, then you now have your own insulin model.

